+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+Addresses the REVIEW.md (round 0) held-out failures. All five findings applied.
+
+- order: pages now come back in the order typed (`"5,1-3"` is `[5, 1, 2, 3]`);
+  the sort is gone from `src/parse-ranges.mjs`.
+- repeats: a page typed twice comes back twice (`"2,2"` is `[2, 2]`); the Set is
+  gone.
+- backward: a range written last-first runs backward (`"5-3"` is `[5, 4, 3]`)
+  instead of throwing.
+- open end: `"8-"` runs to the last page and `"-3"` starts from page 1; a lone
+  `-` still throws a `RangeError`, as do open ends out of bounds (`"0-"`, `"11-"`).
+- empty: an empty or blank text means every page; an empty part between commas
+  (`"1,,2"`, `"1,"`, `",1"`) is still refused.
+
+Along with src/: `tests/parse-ranges.test.mjs` no longer expects sorted,
+deduplicated output, nor throws for backward ranges, open ends or an empty box,
+and has new tests for each; `README.md` documents the new behaviour.
+
+## Round 0
+
+- Added `parseRanges(text, pageCount)`, its tests, and a README.md section.
